 native of the state, he played baseball and football at what is now Oregon State University where he participated in three sports. On the football team, he played three positions and earned the nickname of Ironhorse and all-conference honors. In baseball, he was a right-handed outfielder and after leaving school started his professional career in the minor leagues. Schulmerich then became the first player from the school to make it to the Major Leagues, playing for three teams in the early 1930s. He is a member of the Oregon State University Sports Hall of Fame and the Oregon Sports Hall of Fame.\n\n/home/jinxu/opencode-spawn-pilot/outputs/opencode_spawn_pilot/comparison_v12_single/musique_2hop__657913_88628__single-v12-1777645357/opencode_raw_output.jsonl:\n  Line 3: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1777645868239,\"sessionID\":\"ses_21c0cbf05ffenfjOxGEVqICdh2\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_de3f34980001tcMpPvkKgm3OcK\",\"messageID\":\"msg_de3f3419e001Wnz53LB8f5o2is\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_21c0cbf05ffenfjOxGEVqICdh2\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_a3c28ebdaa9e4bd28a1b60b3\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/jinxu/opencode-spawn-pilot/outputs/opencode_spawn_pilot/comparison_v12_single/.prompt_musique_2hop__657913_88628_1777645357.txt\"},\"output\":\"<path>/home/jinxu/opencode-spawn-pilot/outputs/opencode_spawn_pilot/comparison_v12_single/.prompt_musique_2hop__657913_88628_1777645357.txt</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>1: You are a research agent answering multi-hop questions by searching through documents.\\n2: \\n3: Your task: Read the provided documents, find the information needed to answer the question, and output your answer.\\n4: \\n5: RULES:\\n6: - Use the read and grep tools to search through documents\\n7: - Base your answer ONLY on information found in the documents\\n8: - Do not guess or use your own knowledge\\n9: \\n10: Output your final answer on its own line:\\n11: ANSWER: <your answer>\\n12: \\n13: ---\\n14: \\n15: Answer this multi-hop question using ONLY the provided documents.\\n16: \\n17: Question: Who did the producer of Big Jim McLain play in True Grit?\\n18: \\n19: Documents:\\n20: [Paragraph 0] Granger, Texas\\n21: Granger is a city in Williamson County, Texas, United States. The population was 1,419 at the 2010 census. Granger was the site for the 2010 remake of the movie True Grit, as well as an episode of the NBC drama Revolution.\\n22: \\n23: [Paragraph 1] .700 Nitro Express\\n24: The .700 Nitro Express (17.8×89mmR) is a big game rifle cartridge made by Holland & Holland, London, England. It was developed in 1988 by Jim Bell and William Feldstein and built by H&H. Feldstein had tried unsuccessfully to get H&H to build a .600 Nitro Express for him, but they had already ceased production. However, when Bell and Feldstein ...\n  Line 11: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1777645880657,\"sessionID\":\"ses_21c0cbf05ffenfjOxGEVqICdh2\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_de3f37ea3001IoillzHn359I6m\",\"messageID\":\"msg_de3f36e19001chibXXiXUL2Crl\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_21c0cbf05ffenfjOxGEVqICdh2\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_1af6cb9e5a0e49e7a5c866bf\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"path\":\"/home/jinxu/opencode-spawn-pilot/outputs/opencode_spawn_pilot/comparison_v12_single\",\"pattern\":\"producer|Producer\"},\"output\":\"Found 38 matches\\n/home/jinxu/opencode-spawn-pilot/outputs/opencode_spawn_pilot/comparison_v12_single/musique_2hop__657913_88628__single-v12-1777645357/opencode_raw_output.jsonl:\\n  Line 3: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1777645868239,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_21c0cbf05ffenfjOxGEVqICdh2\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_de3f34980001tcMpPvkKgm3OcK\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_de3f3419e001Wnz53LB8f5o2is\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_21c0cbf05ffenfjOxGEVqICdh2\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"read\\\",\\\"callID\\\":\\\"call_a3c28ebdaa9e4bd28a1b60b3\\\",\\\"state\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/home/jinxu/opencode-spawn-pilot/outputs/opencode_spawn_pilot/comparison_v12_single/.prompt_musique_2hop__657913_88628_1777645357.txt\\\"},\\\"output\\\":\\\"<path>/home/jinxu/opencode-spawn-pilot/outputs/opencode_spawn_pilot/comparison_v12_single/.prompt_musique_2hop__657913_88628_1777645357.txt</path>\\\\n<type>file</type>\\\\n<content>1: You are a research agent answering multi-hop questions by searching through documents.\\\\n2: \\\\n3: Your task: Read the provided documents, find the information needed to answer the question, and output your answer.\\\\n4: \\\\n5: RULES:\\\\n6: - Use the read and grep tools to search through documents\\\\n7: - Base your answer ONLY on information found in the documents\\\\n8: - Do not guess or use your own knowledge\\\\n9: \\\\n10: Output your final answer on its own line:\\\\n11: ANSWER: <your answer>\\\\n12: \\\\n13: ---\\\\n14: \\\\n15: Answer this multi-hop question using ONLY the provided documents.\\\\n16: \\\\n17: Question: Who did t...\n  Line 15: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1777645888528,\"sessionID\":\"ses_21c0cbf05ffenfjOxGEVqICdh2\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_de3f39a77001scpl3vk4WeNASH\",\"messageID\":\"msg_de3f3861c001janPHpzJEXMai8\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_21c0cbf05ffenfjOxGEVqICdh2\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_9e3f1d0d82a64fc58dbb7405\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/jinxu/opencode-spawn-pilot/outputs/opencode_spawn_pilot/comparison_v12_single/musique_2hop__657913_88628__single-v12-1777645357/documents.txt\"},\"output\":\"<path>/home/jinxu/opencode-spawn-pilot/outputs/opencode_spawn_pilot/comparison_v12_single/musique_2hop__657913_88628__single-v12-1777645357/documents.txt</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>1: [Paragraph 0] Granger, Texas\\n2: Granger is a city in Williamson County, Texas, United States. The population was 1,419 at the 2010 census. Granger was the site for the 2010 remake of the movie True Grit, as well as an episode of the NBC drama Revolution.\\n3: \\n4: [Paragraph 1] .700 Nitro Express\\n5: The .700 Nitro Express (17.8×89mmR) is a big game rifle cartridge made by Holland & Holland, London, England. It was developed in 1988 by Jim Bell and William Feldstein and built by H&H. Feldstein had tried unsuccessfully to get H&H to build a .600 Nitro Express for him, but they had already ceased production. However, when Bell and Feldstein produced the entirely new .700 Nitro Express cartridge, they were able to attract the interest of H&H, which was looking for a new big-bore cartridge. After production began, the backlog of orders was so great that it continued to 2007 and H&H restarted the production of .600 Nitro Express guns.\\n6: \\n7: [Paragraph 2] True Grit (1969 film)\\n8: True Grit is a 1969 American western film. It is the first film adaptation of Charles Portis' 1968 novel of the same name. The screenplay was written by Marguerite Roberts. The film was directed by Henry Hathaway and starred Kim Darby as Mattie Ross and John Wayne as U.S. Marshal Rooster Cogburn. Wayne won ...\n\n/home/jinxu/opencode-spawn-pilot/outputs/opencode_spawn_pilot/comparison_v12_single/musique_2hop__657913_88628__single-v12-1777645357/documents.txt:\n  Line 11: The Emancipation of Mimi is the tenth studio album by American singer and songwriter Mariah Carey, released through Island Records on April 12, 2005. \"The Emancipation of Mimi\" was considered Carey's \"comeback album\" by critics and became her highest-selling release in the US in a decade. In composing the album, the singer collaborated with many songwriters and producers throughout 2004, including Jermaine Dupri, Snoop Dogg, Twista, Nelly, Pharrell Williams, and James \"Big Jim\" Wright, many of whom appeared as featured guests on select tracks.\n  Line 35: After ``Normal ''aired, internet sources began to summarize the rules for True American, which the characters described as a mix of a drinking game and Candy Land where the floor is lava; it also involves shouting the names of American presidents. The idea of True American came from a New Girl writer who played a similar game in college. As she could not remember the game's exact rules, the writers focused on making the game as funny on the page as possible, but only established chanting`` JFK! FDR!'' and walking on chairs. As the cast did not understand the game during shooting, the writers created more rules on the spot, advised the actors to ``have fun, dig in, jump in ''and play it as if`` they'd been playing this thing for years and years and years.'' The high - energy feel of the game and the amounts of coverage made filming True American more challenging for the actors than normal episodes. Producers Dave Finkel, Brett Baer, and writer Luvh Rakhe, came up with most of the obscure American history facts, but much was cut from the finished episode. Fox subsequently released a set of official rules for the game, which can be summarized ``There are no real rules ''. The characters also played True American in`` Cooler'', the 15th episode of the second season, in ``Mars Landing '', the 20th episode of the third season and in`` Wedding Eve'' the 21st episode of the fifth season.\n\n/home/jinxu/opencode-spawn-pilot/outputs/opencode_spawn_pilot/comparison_v12_single/musique_2hop__648648_173389__single-v12-1777645357/opencode_raw_output.jsonl:\n  Line 3: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1777645854014,\"sessionID\":\"ses_21c0cf49bffeQpdPODlVdaNvEL\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_de3f31438001o6daXtLlVat6Pf\",\"messageID\":\"msg_de3f30c000017vmBdhM8CPoOnX\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_21c0cf49bffeQpdPODlVdaNvEL\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_30b29890effb48e1b4063f0e\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/jinxu/opencode-spawn-pilot/outputs/opencode_spawn_pilot/comparison_v12_single/.prompt_musique_2hop__648648_173389_1777645357.txt\"},\"output\":